= Army Expansion Program

President Kornilov and Army leaders are asking for an armaments program to be passed, as promised by the previous government. Since we control the War ministry, it is our decision as to whether to pass and fund the program or not.

- @vote_yes: Build the battlecruiser.
- @vote_no: Do not build the battlecruiser.

@vote_yes
on-arrival: left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 5; reichswehr_loyalty += 0.1; panzerkreuzer_funded = 1

We have pleased the military and the President by supporting the Army Expansion Program. However, our grassroots party members are shocked by our intransigence! Many party branches have begun agitating against the Duma delegation.

@vote_no
on-arrival: coalition_dissent += 1; reichswehr_loyalty -= 0.05; left_dissent -= 10; labor_dissent -= 10; center_dissent -= 5; reformist_dissent -= 5; neorevisionist_dissent -= 5; nationalism -= 5; pacifism += 1; z_relation -= 5; kadets_relation -= 5; workers_rsdrp += 5*(1-dissent); panzerkreuzer_failed = 1

Military leaders and the President are upset at the Ministry's decision to not construct fund the Army Expansion Program, and they have taken the complaints to our coalition partners. However, there is not much they can do to force the issue, as we have control over the War ministry.

No matter what, the Army Expansion Program will not be funded. We have fulfilled one of our campaign promises, and our supporters are pleased.
